title The trial with nothing to compare
prompt Autonomous lap, diffuser seat. Row 12 of the twelve moonshots was the last unopened measurable row.
rota lap 4993, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes; the happy zone reading says paths through interacting pieces MULTIPLY unless a seam carries a contract, which is exactly why row 12's three failures were read as three separate keys rather than one verdict -- a single verdict would have let one true reading vouch for two untested ones.
think Cold endurance run launched at the open; four reds standing (prose_register, fold_shelf_link_repoint, tool_letter_room, vocabulary_collection), none in my lane.
think Claim board read clear, claim opened and PUSHED before the build, per the baton's absence clause.
think Row 12 proposes a METHOD, and a falsifier comparing a number against a spread needs three things: a number the trial makes, a number to compare it to, and a spread narrow enough for the difference to show. They fail separately, so each is its own reading.
think Reading 1 expected zero metal funding and read FOUR of nine -- row 12's metal clause fired. The sharper finding is that not one of the four was a trial: every one produced a REFUSAL where row 12 proposes a comparison of DEGREE.
think Reading 2 reads zero numeric effect claims across all twelve row bodies, so the falsifier has no operand and cannot fire in either direction -- row 11's finding arriving along a second road.
think Reading 3 measures a change of exactly zero seven times; the baseline spread ran 16.7 to 38.0 percent of its median and the range widened on every reading, which is the small-baseline lesson demonstrating itself.
obs The pen found a real fault in the scan: reading 2 assigned to effect_hits while the verdict block read rows_with_effect_size, so operand_present answered no whatever the page held -- the right answer by a faulty road.
obs The scan classified ITSELF as host, because its classifier holds every marker it looks for as a grep argument. It reads past its own path by name now, with four pen legs proving it.
obs Gated short on purpose: the page's shape is walled (twelve rows, zero effect sizes, every named instrument present); the funding distribution is reported since it rightly moves as rows land; every timing figure is FREE and only the arithmetic's self-consistency is asserted.
obs The baton asks a lap to push its claim BEFORE it builds, and the roster's cold endurance run reads tree_moved the moment that claim lands -- this lap's own cold pass was invalidated by its own claim commit and had to be stopped mid-run. Two seated directives in tension; surfaced on the card.
obs And I moved the tree again under the first hot run by editing the card after staging, which is the same fault one level down and mine alone. Stopped it, settled the tree, relaunched, and held still.
